  "note": "Independent re-judgment after 562bc0139d against RFC 4271 Section 6.2 (recognized but malformed Optional Parameter: Error Subcode MUST be 0, Unspecific). The NOTIFICATION is 21 octets with empty Data, so notificationWithinPeerLimit (applied in writeMessageHeld to *message.Notification only) returns it unchanged. TestSessionRFC4271OptionalParameterErrors (unchanged) requires the exact reply body [2, 0] and Idle for six malformed inputs: known capability with a wrong length, a truncated capability value, an empty capability parameter, a truncated parameter value and a truncated parameter header; the reply is read by its header Length, so header, code and subcode are all pinned. Negative: a correctly encoded Route Refresh capability reaches OpenConfirm and sends a KEEPALIVE. UnpackOpen's RFC 9072 change (79815edae5) does not reach these Optional Parameters Length values (2-5), and other-commit changes to session_read.go and NewSession would show as a red on the socket bytes, not a false green.",
